WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.147
Morb groaned as he returned to consciousness.

2
00:00:05.148 --> 00:00:09.206
For a moment he didn't remember where he was or what had happened.

3
00:00:09.207 --> 00:00:16.035
Then he saw the ruined house around him and the heavy beam lying beside him. His memory came rushing back.

4
00:00:16.036 --> 00:00:26.152
"Aargh!" he yelled, gnashing his teeth. "Those rotten children will pay for making a fool of me yet again!"

5
00:00:26.153 --> 00:00:29.344
He rubbed his hands together and healed his aching head.

6
00:00:29.345 --> 00:00:32.586
Then he zapped himself back to the fortress.

7
00:00:32.587 --> 00:00:38.841
Several trolls were in the tower room staring dully at the map above the Secret Eye, as Morb had ordered.

8
00:00:38.842 --> 00:00:44.399
Morb glanced at the map, which was still blank. "Ridiculous," he snapped.

9
00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:49.055
Stalking over, he yanked the blink images out of the eye sockets.

10
00:00:49.056 --> 00:00:52.768
Immediately the map filled with glowing red dots.

11
00:00:52.769 --> 00:00:56.278
Morb glared at the trolls, who looked vaguely surprised.

12
00:00:56.279 --> 00:01:02.956
"Don't just stand there looking stupid!" he told them. "Go bring me some more Reds."

13
00:01:02.957 --> 00:01:09.769
The trolls exchanged a glance. One grunted, an image of sloppy gruel appearing over its head.

14
00:01:09.770 --> 00:01:13.914
"You'll get more food when you've earned it," Morb snapped.

15
00:01:13.915 --> 00:01:19.602
"Go!" He waited until the trolls zapped away, and then stomped downstairs.

16
00:01:19.603 --> 00:01:22.905
Boz was lying in his cell, weak and pale.

17
00:01:22.906 --> 00:01:28.998
Two trolls were coming out of the cell, carrying a large cauldron full of the bright blue leeches.

18
00:01:28.999 --> 00:01:33.409
"I hope you enjoyed today's treatment," Morb said sarcastically.

19
00:01:33.410 --> 00:01:39.498
"Normally I give my guests a day off to regain their magical energy between treatments.

20
00:01:39.499 --> 00:01:45.846
But since you are a former Magic Master, I thought you could handle two days in a row."

21
00:01:45.847 --> 00:01:49.871
Boz barely had the energy to lift his head and glare at Morb.

22
00:01:49.872 --> 00:01:53.236
"You won't get away with this," he croaked.

23
00:01:53.237 --> 00:01:58.099
"Don't try to talk too much, my friend," Morb warned with a sneer.

24
00:01:58.100 --> 00:02:03.371
"You need to rest before your next treatment. My leeches are always hungry.

25
00:02:03.372 --> 00:02:10.158
If you don't provide enough magic, they just might suck the life out of you one of these times."

26
00:02:10.159 --> 00:02:14.118
"Is that supposed to be a threat?" Boz said.

27
00:02:14.119 --> 00:02:18.214
"Because you don't scare me, Morb. You never did."

28
00:02:18.215 --> 00:02:25.273
"We'll see if you're still so confident when your grandson is in the cell next to you," Morb snarled.

29
00:02:25.274 --> 00:02:30.212
"Zann?" Panic suddenly filled Boz's face. "Is he here?"

30
00:02:30.213 --> 00:02:38.079
Morb didn't answer. Instead he turned and walked out of the cell, ordering the trolls to bring the cauldron of leeches.

31
00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:44.951
Boz continued to yell, but Morb ignored him and went into a small room at the end of the corridor.

32
00:02:44.952 --> 00:02:49.381
Inside was a stone pit full of firewood and kindling.

33
00:02:49.382 --> 00:02:52.960
Morb pointed, and instantly flames leaped out.

34
00:02:52.961 --> 00:02:56.861
With a grunt the trolls lifted the cauldron onto the fire.

35
00:02:56.862 --> 00:03:02.743
As the leeches cooked, the magic energy they had just ingested left their bodies.

36
00:03:02.744 --> 00:03:07.843
It rose up like steam, emerging from the cauldron in thick blue spirals.

37
00:03:07.844 --> 00:03:12.000
Morb leaned over the cauldron, breathing in the escaping magic. The

38
00:03:12.001 --> 00:03:16.867
steam burned his nose and throat, but he ignored the unpleasant feeling. For

39
00:03:16.868 --> 00:03:22.455
now he would continue to do things the slow, difficult way. But not for much longer. He

40
00:03:22.456 --> 00:03:27.332
was almost strong enough to put the next step of his plan into action. "Yes,"

41
00:03:27.333 --> 00:03:36.015
he whispered, inhaling deeply, as more and more magical energy filled him. He

42
00:03:36.016 --> 00:03:39.396
felt powerful—more powerful than ever before. Boz

43
00:03:39.397 --> 00:03:43.877
had strong magic indeed. And now it was all his! Morb

44
00:03:43.878 --> 00:03:46.823
breathed in the last of the blue steam. Then

45
00:03:46.824 --> 00:03:56.793
he threw back his head and laughed, never noticing the big-eyed insect fluttering outside the tiny barred window at the top of the stone wall. "So

46
00:03:56.794 --> 00:04:01.637
your grandfather was suspicious of Morb from the start?" Gliss asked. Zann

47
00:04:01.638 --> 00:04:06.968
looked around at his friends. All of them, plus Zing, were still in the Hollow. They

48
00:04:06.969 --> 00:04:13.409
hadn't heard from Jev yet. So Zann was still reading as much as he could from his grandfather's diary. "Boz

49
00:04:13.410 --> 00:04:19.468
was suspicious of Morb," he said. "At least that's what he wrote in here. Boz

50
00:04:19.469 --> 00:04:27.213
stopped by the university a few days after Morb started working as an assistant animal caretaker at my parents' lab. At

51
00:04:27.214 --> 00:04:31.540
first Boz just thought Morb seemed secretive and shifty." "And

52
00:04:31.541 --> 00:04:33.927
then what?" Perda asked. "One

53
00:04:33.928 --> 00:04:41.572
day Boz caught Morb performing some nasty secret research on the lab animals," he said. Perda

54
00:04:41.573 --> 00:04:44.961
gasped. "What was he doing?" "Boz

55
00:04:44.962 --> 00:04:51.538
guessed that Morb was trying to figure out ways to steal magic from the creatures under his care." Darb

56
00:04:51.539 --> 00:04:57.444
looked stricken. "That's terrible!" he said, reaching out to stroke Zing's scales. "That

57
00:04:57.445 --> 00:05:02.209
sort of experimentation is strictly regulated by the Red Council. And

58
00:05:02.210 --> 00:05:06.084
caretakers are never supposed to take part in it." "I

59
00:05:06.085 --> 00:05:10.631
know," Zann said. "But I guess Morb didn't care. The

60
00:05:10.632 --> 00:05:15.516
second time Boz caught him, he was eating some leeches." "

61
00:05:15.517 --> 00:05:19.525
Eating them?" Gliss shuddered. "Yuck!"

62
00:05:19.526 --> 00:05:23.534
Zann nodded. "I guess it worked, at least a little.

63
00:05:23.535 --> 00:05:29.335
Morb was able to do enough magic to zap himself away before Boz could stop him."

64
00:05:29.336 --> 00:05:31.896
"What did Boz do?" Darb asked.

65
00:05:31.897 --> 00:05:37.919
"He told my parents that they should fire Morb and report him to the Council."

66
00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:39.112
"Did they?"

67
00:05:39.113 --> 00:05:43.777
"The next few pages aren't in very good shape." Zann bit his lip.

68
00:05:43.778 --> 00:05:46.437
"So I'm not sure what happened after that.

69
00:05:46.438 --> 00:05:52.132
The next part that's readable talks about Boz and me moving to Swamp Bottom."

70
00:05:52.133 --> 00:06:00.369
"Wow." Perda looked thoughtful. "Don't you find it odd that all that stuff happened right before your parents disappeared?"

71
00:06:00.370 --> 00:06:06.272
Zann shot her a look. "Are you saying that Morb had something to do with my parents' disappearance too?"

72
00:06:06.273 --> 00:06:10.176
Just then they heard Jev calling them from outside the Hollow.

73
00:06:10.177 --> 00:06:22.597
Perda jumped to her feet. "The spy fly must be back," she cried. "Let's go find out what it saw!"

